{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And to Moshe He said — Moshe ascended to the cloud where Elohim was, and YHWH said to Moshe: Thus shall you say to the children of Israel. All these passages up to here were on the day they heard the Ten Commandments. 'And to Moshe He said' — to him alone, at the time of his descent, on that very day." "Ascend to YHWH — on the next day." "You and Aharon, etc. — and afterwards Moshe immediately descended — 'and he told the people all the words of YHWH,' etc. And afterwards he descended, and on the next day built an altar and offered sacrifices, and on that very day he ascended — 'and the cloud covered it six days,' etc." "And to Moshe He said — an angel." "Ascend to YHWH — since it did not write 'to Me,' as is written further on: ״עלה אלי ההרה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The first sentence appears to be a narrative paraphrase; the phrase מומשה appears to read 'from Moshe' but contextually means 'Moshe'; translated hyper-literally as 'Moshe ascended.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:55.776096286Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}